# The seven members `kneemri-relabel7` ships, and NOTHING ELSE.
#
# A package of its own rather than a version bump of `kneemri-members`, because the live members
# dataset is 13 GB of 120 checkpoints and this entry names seven of them. Re-uploading 13 GB to add
# one 89 MB file spends an hour of wall-clock and puts the CHAMPION's serving dataset through a
# version bump for an instrument entry — a cost and a risk that buy nothing this entry needs.
#
# `MemberPackage.find` takes the FIRST manifest it walks to, so a kernel reading this package must
# mount it and NOT `kneemri-members`; two mounted packages make which one serves an accident of walk
# order. `kneemri-relabel7`'s metadata names this one alone.
#
# The first six are the champion's seats, unchanged, so the entry's delta is the seventh member's own
# contribution and not a difference against a re-selected six.
final_ws_cf.pt
calib_span_ff.pt
grade_ladder_cf.pt
merged_blend_cf.pt
lr4e-5_ws_cf.pt
through_dense_cf.pt
# The seventh: the only member this project owns whose TRUTH differs from every other member's —
# fitted against a label table with 1,932 cells corrected by a confident-learning detector.
errors_relabel_s2026.pt
